  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J1", "U2", "R10"],
      "pins": ["J1.3", "U2.7"],
      "nets": ["RESET", "NRST"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet the MCU reset pin U2.7 and its pull-up R10 sit on the net labelled 'NRST', but the Tag-Connect header pin J1.3 is attached to a different net label, 'RESET'. Because the two carry different global/hierarchical label names, no wire connects them, so J1.3 is left as a single-pin (floating) net.",
      "expected": "The specification states the reset line must be shared: 'R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC ... NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}) so the Tag-Connect programmer can pull it low.' J1.3 should therefore be on the same net as U2.7/R10 (i.e. labelled NRST).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet, 'Programming (SWD)' block: J1 pin 3 carries the red net label 'RESET'; MCU block: U2 pin 7 (NRST) and R10 carry the red net label 'NRST'."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Reset line: R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC ... NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}) so the Tag-Connect programmer can pull it low."}
      ],
      "impact": "The SWD/Tag-Connect programmer cannot assert the MCU's external reset pin; the J1 reset pad is unconnected to the MCU reset net. Board boot/reset behaviour is unchanged, but the documented programming interface loses its hardware-reset capability.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All component values, types, I2C/TSC/charge-pump/antenna connections and power rails match the specification, but the Tag-Connect reset pin J1.3 is labelled 'RESET' while the MCU reset net is labelled 'NRST', leaving the programmer's reset line disconnected from the MCU contrary to the spec."
}

